permalink: /blog/search.json
layout: null
---
{%- comment -%}
  Search index for the blog filter, consumed by initBlogSearch() in
  assets/javascript/dbz.js.

  Why an index rather than filtering the DOM: the FAQ filter hides sections that
  are all already on the page, but the blog is paginated ten posts at a time
  across 351 posts. Filtering the DOM would search ten of them and report "no
  results" for a post sitting on page twelve.

  Scope is metadata plus a capped excerpt, deliberately not post bodies. Bodies
  roughly triple the payload and make matching worse rather than better: the
  word "oracle" appears in 201 post bodies, and 174 of the 183 posts tagged
  `oracle` are release announcements carrying a roll-call of every connector
  touched. A connector name is close to meaningless as a filter on this blog,
  which is also why the ranking in the JavaScript weights titles far above tags.

  The excerpt is capped at `listing.excerpt_words` rather than cut at
  `excerpt_separator`. 24 of the 351 posts have no separator, and Jekyll falls
  back to the entire body when a custom separator is not found - those 24 bodies
  come to 222KB on their own, one of them 35KB.

  Every value goes through `jsonify`, which quotes and escapes it. Post titles
  contain quotes and colons, so hand-writing the quotes would produce invalid
  JSON for a good number of them.

  `site.posts` is newest first, and the order is preserved so the client can
  show results in date order without sorting.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign cfg = site.data.blog.listing -%}
[
{%- for post in site.posts -%}
{%- comment -%}
  Four posts credit several authors as a comma separated list with inconsistent
  spacing, hence the `remove: " "`. Ids are downcased to match the directories
  _plugins/authors.rb creates, while the display lookup uses the id unchanged
  because authors.yaml is keyed as written in front matter.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign authorIds = post.author | remove: " " | split: "," -%}
{"title":{{ post.title | jsonify }},"url":{{ post.url | prepend: site.baseurl | jsonify }},"date":{{ post.date | date: "%Y-%m-%d" | jsonify }},"authors":[
{%- for authorId in authorIds -%}{{ authorId | downcase | jsonify }}{% unless forloop.last %},{% endunless %}{%- endfor -%}
],"authorNames":[
{%- for authorId in authorIds -%}
{%- assign entry = site.data.authors[authorId] -%}
{% if entry.name %}{{ entry.name | jsonify }}{% else %}{{ authorId | jsonify }}{% endif %}{% unless forloop.last %},{% endunless %}
{%- endfor -%}
],"tags":{{ post.tags | jsonify }},"excerpt":{{ post.content | strip_html | remove: "+++" | normalize_whitespace | truncatewords: cfg.excerpt_words | jsonify }}}{% unless forloop.last %},{% endunless %}
{%- endfor -%}
]
